.TH NOVNC-SESSIONS.YAML 5 "2026-10-29" "mu2edaq-shifter-tools" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
novnc-sessions.yaml \- descriptions and card order for the noVNC session dashboard
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I config/novnc-sessions.yaml
.br
.I ~/.config/mu2edaq/novnc-sessions.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBClient side.\fR
.BR start-novnc-connection.sh (1)
reads this file on your laptop when it builds the session dashboard. It
gives each VNC session a description and puts the cards in order.
.PP
The file is a YAML mapping whose key \fBgroups\fR holds a list of
groups. Each group is drawn under its label, with a separator line
between groups, and \fBgroups and cards appear in the order of the
file.\fR A group is a mapping with these keys:
.TP
.B label
Heading shown above the group. Optional.
.TP
.B sessions
List of sessions, described below. Required; a group without it is
reported and skipped.
.PP
For backward compatibility a file may instead have a flat top-level
\fBsessions\fR list, which is one unlabeled group. A file with both
uses \fBgroups\fR and says so.
.PP
A session on the tunnel host (the noVNC portal's host) must be one the
portal offers, since the portal supplies its browser link; an entry the
portal does not offer is reported on standard error and skipped. A
session on \fBany other host\fR gets a card of its own. It has no browser
link, because the portal serves only its own host, and, when it has a
\fBdisplay\fR, a native VNC link through an ssh to that host. Portal
sessions the file does not name follow at the end: in the last group
when no group has a label, otherwise in a group labeled "Other sessions
on \fIhost\fR".
.PP
Each session is a mapping with these keys:
.TP
.B account
Login account, exactly as the portal's session list names it, for
example \fBmu2eshift\fR. Required; an entry without it is skipped with a
warning.
.TP
.B description
What the desktop is for, in a sentence or two. Shown under the host.
HTML in it is escaped, not rendered.
.TP
.B display
X display number of the session on its host. When given, the card
shows \fIhost\fB:\fIdisplay\fR, and, for a session on the tunnel host,
.BR start-novnc-connection.sh (1)
forwards a local port to 5900+\fIdisplay\fR so the card can offer a
native VNC link. Display numbers are not account
numbers; on mu2e-mgr-01, \fBmu2ecr0\fIN\fR is display \fIN\fR+3.
.TP
.B host
Host running the session. Default: the host the tunnel goes to
(\fBNOVNC_HOST\fR, normally \fImu2e\-mgr\-01.fnal.gov\fR). The same
account may appear on several hosts; a session is identified by
\fIaccount\fB@\fIhost\fR.
.TP
.B ssh_user
For a session on another host: the login for the ssh that carries its
native forward. Default: whatever your ssh configuration says
(\fI~/.ssh/config_mu2e\fR logs \fBmu2e\-mc1\-cr\-*\fR in as
\fBmu2eshift\fR).
.TP
.B jump
For a session on another host: ProxyJump host for that ssh. Default:
your ssh configuration.
.PP
Other keys are ignored.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
The file is read with PyYAML (\fByaml.safe_load\fR) in the
\fBpython3\fR on your \fBPATH\fR. Without PyYAML the dashboard still
renders, in portal order and with no descriptions, and one warning
says how to install it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python3 \-m pip install \-\-user pyyaml
.fi
.RE
.PP
A file that cannot be parsed, or has no \fBsessions\fR list, is
likewise reported and ignored. Problems with this file never stop the
dashboard from opening.
.SH FILES
The file used is the first found of: the \fB\-c\fR option, then
\fBNOVNC_SESSIONS_FILE\fR, then \fBnovnc-sessions.yaml\fR in
\fI./config\fR, the checkout's \fIconfig/\fR, \fI~/.config/mu2edaq\fR
and \fI/etc/mu2edaq\fR. A CMake install puts the shipped copy in
\fI<prefix>/share/mu2edaq/config\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
groups:
  \- label: mu2e\-mgr\-01 (MC\-2)
    sessions:
      \- account: mu2eshift
        display: 2
        description: Shift crew main desktop.
      \- account: mu2edcs
        display: 1
        description: Detector Control System desktop.
  \- label: MC\-1 Control Room
    sessions:
      \- account: mu2eshift
        host: mu2e\-mc1\-cr\-01.fnal.gov
        display: 2
        description: MC\-1 control room console 1.
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check which file a run would use without opening anything:
.PP
.RS
.nf
scripts/start\-novnc\-connection.sh \-n
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR start-novnc-connection.sh (1),
.BR install\-ssh\-config.sh (1)
